# The build context is the repo root, because the image needs `agent/` (which carries the
# packages) and `domains/`. These are the parts it never needs, and
# sending them is pure cost on a Pi.
#
# NOTE: onboarding/ is deliberately NOT ignored here. Excluding it from the context would hide
# the boundary in a file nobody reads; it is excluded by the Containerfile not naming it, where
# a test can see the decision. See tests/test_layout.py.

.git
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Firmware is flashed to a board, never built into an image; a generated include/config.h
# carries the wifi and a device credential, and must never reach a layer.
firmware

# an agent's belief base is created at birth, never baked in
**/state

# secrets are MOUNTED per world, never copied into a layer
world/*/secrets
keys

# not needed at runtime
# The agent's packages carry their tests beside their code.
**/tests
**/test_*.py
knowledge
infra/grafana
infra/mosquitto
